From 7e9fe015835f156a7903945b19c3af3c33ec64c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ishneet Ahuja <ishneet@google.com>
Date: Thu, 21 May 2026 11:33:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] RESTRICT AUTOMERGE Improve preselcted media URI
 validation

The photopicker allows apps to pass URIs of media items that they
already have access to via EXTRA_PICKER_PRE_SELECTION_URIS.
This change makes validation of these passed URIs more stringent.

This change adds the following checks:
- A check to ensure that user ID encoded within
  each URI matches the current active user profile. This ensures that preselected
  media remains consistent with the active profile and prevents any data mismatch
  during database queries.
- Checks the Uri scheme. It should be a content URI.
- Checks that all the segments of the Uri are as expected of a valid
  picker URI. We use LocalUriMatcher for this check.

Bug: 471796999,471797062

Test: atest PickerDataLayerV2Test PickerUriResolverTest

Flag: EXEMPT CVE_FIX
Change-Id: I7bf6d97a7fac3ecc708df96a93363cbb3e512216
